     "en": "A short story"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "Meena saw the railway lines running side by side and a road crossing them.\n\"Some lines never meet,\" she said."
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "explain",
    "type": "explanation",
    "provenance": "original",
    "keepEnglishTerms": [
     "parallel",
     "perpendicular",
     "protractor"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "Parallel lines never meet however far they go. Intersecting lines cross at a point. Perpendicular lines meet at a right angle of 90 degrees.\nWe measure an angle with a protractor. Place its centre on the vertex and line up one arm with zero, then read the other arm.\nAngles are right (90), acute (less than 90), obtuse (between 90 and 180) and straight (180)."
    }
   },
